  "text": "Recipe: Steamed Bean Dumplings\nCreator: Gurmeet Manku\nCategory: Dumplings\nIngredients: toor dal, fresh mint, cilantro, cumin powder, ginger powder, black pepper, cardamom powder, tomatoes, red onion, avocado, lemon, dried berry medley, cranberries, golden berries, mulberries, goji berries, various dried berries, various herbs & spices\nCooking methods: no-cook, blend, steam\nInstructions: DUMPLINGS: Soak toor dal overnight. Drain all water. Combine with some fresh mint, cilantro & spices like cumin powder, ginger powder, black pepper & cardamom powder. Turn into paste with high speed blender. Make interesting ball-like shapes and steam in a steamer. DRESSING: Make a salsa-like dressing with tomatoes, red onion, cilantro, avocado, lemon & black pepper. Optionally add dried berry medley (cranberries, golden berries, mulberries, goji berries, ...) soaked in water for some time.\nNotes: Sub-recipes: DUMPLINGS, DRESSING. Ingredient summary: BEANS (toor dal), RAINBOW VEGGIES (tomato, red onion), BERRIES (various dried berries), LIME-LEMON-VINEGAR (lemon), HERBS & SPICES (various).",
